Found during the 0.500 pre-release audit (karr-release-checker).

Changes lines 387-402 ("Fixed a remote that is empty for the wrong reason
reconciling the whole board away...") ends: "Only the total wipe is guarded:
a pull that leaves at least one board ref standing still reconciles
unattended, so a remote swapped for a different, non-empty board is not
caught."

That is exactly the gap ticket #95 was filed for -- and #95 is already closed:
Changes lines 167-183 ("Fixed the wipe guard's blind spot...") documents the
fix, via refs/karr/meta/board-id: "it caught a remote that had lost every
board ref, but not one swapped for a DIFFERENT non-empty board ... Boards now
carry an identity ... A pull where both sides have an id and they differ is
refused before any reconciliation."

So within the current unreleased {{$NEXT}} block, one entry states a
limitation as still open while another entry, earlier in the same block,
closes exactly that limitation. Same shape as the #38/#105 contradiction that
was already cleaned up today. The stale sentence at Changes:400-402 should be
removed or updated (e.g. point at the #95 fix instead of restating the old
gap) before release.

Not a code bug -- a Changes-file accuracy issue. Blocks release only in the
sense that the changelog should not contradict itself.
